        "Arsenic: **0.01 mg/L**, with no relaxation - arsenic is a proven carcinogen, so no economic argument buys a higher limit. [IS 10500:2012]",
        "Iron 0.3 mg/L; TDS 500 mg/L acceptable, 2000 mg/L permissible - the permissible figure applies only where no alternative source exists. [IS 10500:2012]",
        "Total hardness 200 mg/L acceptable and 600 mg/L permissible, as calcium carbonate. [IS 10500:2012]",
        "pH **6.5-8.5**; turbidity 1 NTU acceptable, 5 NTU permissible - turbid water shields organisms from chlorine. [IS 10500:2012]",
        "Residual chlorine **at least 0.2 mg/L at the consumer's tap** - it proves the whole distribution line, not just the plant, stayed safe. [IS 10500:2012]",
        "Viral water-borne infections: hepatitis A and E, rotavirus, polio - hepatitis E is the one that kills pregnant women. [Park 27e]",
        "Bacterial water-borne infections: typhoid, cholera, shigella, E. coli - all are killed by chlorine at a normal residual. [Park 27e]",
