        "Helminthic: guinea worm - India was certified free in **February 2000**. [Park 27e]",
        "**Fluorosis** is the chemical hazard of Rajasthan, Telangana and Andhra Pradesh - deep groundwater there dissolves fluoride from rock. [Park 27e]",
        "**Arsenicosis** in the Gangetic belt: raindrop pigmentation, keratosis, skin and bladder cancer - the cancers appear decades after exposure. [Park 27e]",
        "Nitrate in shallow wells causes infant methaemoglobinaemia - the blue baby of well water. [Park 27e]",
        "**Jal Jeevan Mission**, August 2019, gives every rural home a tap connection - a shared source is recontaminated on the way home. [JJM 2019]",
        "JJM service level is **55 litres per capita per day** - enough for drinking, cooking and the washing that prevents skin and eye disease. [JJM 2019]",
        "Rural tap coverage rose from **17% of households in 2019 to about 80% by early 2025** - the measure is functional taps, not pipelines laid. [JJM 2019]",
        "Ask about the source and storage of water in every diarrhoea and jaundice consultation - the sanitary survey starts in the clinic.",
        "**Temporary hardness** comes from bicarbonates and is removed by **boiling** - heat drives off carbon dioxide and precipitates the carbonate. [Park 27e]",
