        "Standard: **free residual chlorine 0.5 mg/L after one hour of contact** - both the level and the hour are needed for a kill. [Park 27e]",
        "Raise to **1 mg/L** when viral disease such as hepatitis is feared - viruses need more chlorine than bacteria. [Park 27e]",
        "**Break point chlorination** is the dose at which all chloramine is oxidised and free chlorine appears - only free chlorine disinfects reliably. [Park 27e]",
