        "**PERT is probabilistic, event-oriented and time-based**, used where durations are uncertain - research and development, or any first-time project. [Park 27e]",
        "PERT takes **three time estimates - optimistic (to), most likely (tm) and pessimistic (tp)**. [Park 27e]",
        "**Expected time te = (to + 4tm + tp) / 6** - the most likely estimate is weighted four times. [Park 27e]",
        "**Standard deviation = (tp - to) / 6** and **variance = [(tp - to) / 6] squared**. [Park 27e]",
        "Along the critical path the **variances are added and the square root gives the project standard deviation**. [Park 27e]",
        "**Z = (scheduled time minus expected time) / project standard deviation**, read against the normal table for the probability of finishing by a date. [Park 27e]",
