    "**Painless haematuria in a dye, rubber, leather or printing worker** - transitional cell carcinoma of the bladder from beta-naphthylamine or benzidine until proved otherwise, even decades after the job ended; send urine cytology and refer for cystoscopy and imaging rather than treating a presumed urinary infection.",
